      "kind": "instruction",
      "path": "/home/jhx/combination_coverage/results/failure_analysis/deepswe_failed_trials_n211_20261006/trials/bandit-structured-nosec-directiv__d8HxTvf/instruction.md",
      "sha256": "310eeb36b46c3aece39ab187817b87764f0a428affe5e8a1688e0c92f7b92f9d",
      "bytes": 2821,
      "line_count": 18,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "Bandit can suppress findings with inline # nosec, but it cannot currently suppress a whole span of code or just the next statement without repeating inline markers. Add directives for region suppression and next-statement suppression."
        },
        {
          "line": 2,
          "text": "Directive keywords are matched case-insensitively. Each directive accepts an optional selector argument written directly after the directive keyword with no keyword prefix (e.g. # nosec-begin B602, # nosec-next-line B602)."
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "Selector syntax:"
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "If omitted or empty, all tests are suppressed. The special token all also suppresses all tests; none means the directive has no effect and no suppression is applied."
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "Tokens may be test IDs or test names. Test IDs may include a glob wildcard to match multiple IDs by prefix."
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "Tokens separated by spaces or commas are unioned. The operators | (union), & (intersection), - (difference), and ! (negation relative to the full enabled test set) are supported, with parentheses for grouping."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "If the expression cannot be parsed, fall back to treating all whitespace and comma-separated tokens as a plain union."
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "# nosec-begin [SELECTOR]: Start a suppression region for subsequent physical lines. The directive line itself is not suppressed, and the begin takes effect starting on the next line after the directive (it is not retroactive). If a region begin directive appears on an indented line and is not explic"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "# nosec-end: End the most recently started active region before the line containing this directive. Extra text after nosec-end is ignored. Unmatched end directives do nothing."
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": "# Note: Suppressions are statement-wide. If a multi-line statement has any suppressed line, findings for that statement are suppressed even if a # nosec-end appears on a later line within the same statement."
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "# nosec-next-line [SELECTOR]: Suppress findings for the next statement after the directive. When locating the target statement, skip blank lines, comment-only lines, and lines containing only grouping tokens ((, ), [, ], {, }), semicolons, or ellipsis literals (...)."
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "All directive types must be ignored when Bandit is run with ignore-nosec enabled."
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "All applicable suppressions for a finding must be combined. If any applicable suppression is blanket, it dominates."
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "Metrics: Blanket suppression increments nosec; specific suppression increments skipped_tests. Classification is based on the resolved set: if the result is a blanket suppression, it counts as nosec; if it resolves to a non-empty specific set, it counts as skipped_tests."
        },
        {
          "line": 18,
          "text": "IMPORTANT: Please work on this in a new branch from main and commit everything when you are done."
        }
      ]
    },
